#====================================================================
# Draft - OHOS-target qmake binaries cannot run as Windows host tools
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-algobox-ohos-target-qmake-windows-host
trigger_tool:           conan_create|qmake|python|runtime
phase:                  configuration|compilation|testing
error_signature:        WinError 193|not a valid Win32 application|The system cannot execute the specified program|qmake6 binary|No QTextCodec header found|QtCore5Compat/QTextCodec|QWebChannel file not found|expected expression|msg.split|Core5Compat.so|Unknown module(s) in QT: core5compat

severity:               2
category:               host-toolchain|qt|qmake|cross-target|webengine-fallback
match_keywords:         qmake6, Windows host, OHOS-target binary, WinError 193, host tool, Conan graph, Qt package, QTextCodec, QStringDecoder, QStringEncoder, QWebChannel, qtwebchannel, QTextBrowser fallback, escaped newline, C++ string literal, local shim, Core5Compat, qmake module
title:                  OHOS-target qmake binaries cannot run as Windows host tools

root_cause:             Conan can resolve qtbase/6.11.1 and expose qmake6, but that executable is built for the OHOS target ABI. A Windows host can inspect the package and resolve its dependency graph, yet cannot execute the target binary as a build tool.
affected_scope:         qmake-based Qt packages whose build recipe pulls qmake from an OHOS-target dependency package or any other non-host executable tool package.
verification_cmd:       python -c "import subprocess; subprocess.run([qmake6, '-v'], check=True)"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           host-native-tool-or-runner-only-validation
rec_description:        Keep Windows-host work limited to source inspection, dependency graph resolution, and metadata validation. Run the full qmake build only on a host that can execute the tool, or switch the recipe to a host-native qmake package if one is available.
rec_command:            On Windows host, stop after conan graph info; on OHOS-compatible runner, execute the full conan create flow.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               host-runner-validation-boundary

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      graph-check-only-with-runner-handoff
fallback_description:   If no host-native qmake is available, treat the Windows-host result as dependency resolution only and hand the full build to an OHOS-compatible runner instead of retrying the same executable.
fallback_command:       Record the unresolved host-tool mismatch and move the build step to a runnable environment.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          runner-handoff

forbid_1_pattern:       WinError 193|not a valid Win32 application|cannot execute the specified program
forbid_1_reason:        A target binary cannot become runnable by rerunning the same host-side command.
forbid_1_consequence:   Repeating qmake6 on Windows returns the same host-tool mismatch and hides the real fix path.
forbid_2_pattern:       conan graph info.*enough|dependency graph.*means.*build.*ready|graph resolution.*success.*tool.*runnable
forbid_2_reason:        Graph resolution does not prove that a packaged executable can run on the build host.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package appears ready until the first build-tool invocation fails.

principles:             P013

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

